<p>What keeps the &quot;Jerry Siegal&quot; thing from breaking it for me is that the comics <em>aren't</em> about 4128. Neither the comic books nor the character are anomalous, they are still the product of the creators' imaginations. One inexplicable sight and one bullshit comment were just the spark that got the imagination going &#8212; not a substitute for it.</p>
<p>I also like the life-imitating-art-imitating-life aspect of 4128 trying to live up to the &quot;Superman&quot; mythos (and failing, because he's only human, and doesn't have writers that make sure everything works out in the end.)</p>

