					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/augmentedspartan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1775542); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1775542&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238202" alt="augmentedspartan" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1775542)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/augmentedspartan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1775542); return false;" >augmentedspartan</a></span> <span class="odate time_1555197292 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Apr 2019 23:14</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4218250">
									

<p>I was a bit hesitant at first because of the obvious Unbreakable inspiration this has, to the point that it almost felt like a copy. Thankfully, this went beyond that and actually touched upon something I think Unbreakable failed to: actually having real world consequences in vigilantism. Bruce Willis beating up a rapist/murderer is good for a first step, but we never got to see how he dealt with toning back his strength or dealing with the law or the aftermath of his actions. I also liked how the SCPs mistake wasn't getting pissed and beating a rapist or serial killer to death, but rather being startled and messing up. It feels more grounded.</p>
<p>That being said, my biggest beef with this is something that pops up a lot in some articles. Convoluted language =/= professionalism. Having the interviewer use unnecessarily complicated jargon doesn't make them seem genuine, but rather a pretentious ass for using <em>&quot;Do you possess the ability of anatomical aviation?&quot;</em> instead of <em>&quot;can you fly?&quot;</em> like any normal person. Seriously, psychologists and psychiatrists don't talk like some b-movie scientists. They want to understand their patient, not assert their intellectual superiority. Overall the interviewing Dr. felt really dry and emotionless, and took me out of an otherwise pretty good story.</p>
<p>Novote</p>

							</div>

								
					
